    body: '# 2c Washington plate proof


      ## Description

      - **Description:** Certified plate proofs are the last printed proof of the plate before printing the stamps at the
      Bureau of Engraving and Printing. These plate proofs are each unique, with the approval signatures and date. For postal
      scholars these plates provide important production information in the plate margin inscriptions, including guidelines,
      plate numbers, and initials of the siderographer, or person who created the plate from a transfer roll.

      - **Description:** Plate No. 10

      - **Description:** Denomination: 2 c

      - **Description:** Subject: Washington

      - **Description:** Color: pink


      ## Names

      - **Printer:** Bureau of Engraving and Printing


      ## Identifier

      - **Object number:** 0.242263.10


      ## Set

      - **See more items in:** National Postal Museum Collection


      ## Object Type

      - **Type:** Bureau Plate Proofs


      ## Physical

      - **Medium:** paper; ink (pink) /engraving'
